<section class="narrow article page-heading"><span class="eyebrow">About SchemePath</span><h1>Clearer scheme information, with limits made visible.</h1><p>SchemePath is an independent educational project for browsing structured public-support scheme information and testing profile details against saved rules.</p><h2>How matching works</h2><p>Rules are stored in the database as approved profile attributes, operators, and values. Conditions inside a group are joined with AND or OR, and groups are joined using the scheme-level operator. Missing data is shown as unknown. The application does not make official decisions.</p><h2>Data quality</h2><p>Records marked DEMO ONLY are fictional and exist to exercise application behavior. Unverified records have not been confirmed against an official source. Administrators should record a source and review date before presenting a scheme as verified.</p><h2>Decision disclaimer</h2><p>Assessments are preliminary and are not official government approval or a guarantee of benefits. Confirm current rules and application requirements with the relevant official authority.</p></section>
